{"work_id":"tirumbippaar","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":47,"scene_status":"corrected-source-reconciled","unit_count":23,"units":[{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u023","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(He opens the table drawer and takes out a revolver.)","notes":["This source-visible action begins scene 47; it was historically attached to scene 46 and is restored here without renumbering existing units."]}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u001","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(Pandiyan and Kumudha are asleep from exhaustion. Paranthaman comes, fires, and runs away; the shot hits the large mirror. Pandiyan and Kumudha wake and cling to each other in fear.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u002","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(Paranthaman runs down the stairs. Hearing the sound, Poomalai comes crying 'Kumudha, Kumudha' and meets him on the staircase.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u003","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d001","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Paranthaman! You sinner! What have you done!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u004","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d002","speaker_label":"பரந்தாமன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Leave me. In this world Paranthaman must have neither enemies nor people who are of no use to him!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u005","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(He says this and leaves in fury.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u006","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d003","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Kumudha! Kumudha!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u007","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(She runs upstairs.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u008","kind":"stage-direction","status":"verified","source":{"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(Kumudha's room.)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u009","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d004","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"(Screaming) Kumudha..."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u010","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d005","speaker_label":"குமுதா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Chinnamma... (embracing her)"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u011","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d006","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Someone has tried to kill me."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u012","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d007","speaker_label":"குமுதா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":53}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Who else could it be? It is the enemy within our own house, Chinnamma! Either we must leave this house, or your brother must leave."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u013","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d008","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"What right do you or I have to tell him to leave?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u014","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d009","speaker_label":"குமுதா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"So you have the right only to let my husband be murdered?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u015","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d010","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Kumudha! What is this!"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u016","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d011","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Let her speak. Let her speak. She alone was left! Once she too has spoken, what more is left for me?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u017","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d012","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Pandiyan! Please listen to what I say. You and Kumudha should leave this town for a few days...."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u018","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d013","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Out of fear of death? Uh-uh..."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u019","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d014","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"For my Kumudha. So that the flower-grove swaying in her hair is not destroyed, grant me this one boon, Pandiyan. My Kumudha has never even touched suffering. I know that even if she were cut into pieces, you are the great medicine that could join them again without breaking continuity. I will not allow that medicine, Kumudha's feast of happiness, to be destroyed. Please. I sacrificed my love for you, did I not? (Kumudha action.) In the name of that sacrifice, in the name of that love, I ask you. I beg you. Agree."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u020","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d015","speaker_label":"குமுதா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Chinnamma... (runs to her)."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u021","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d016","speaker_label":"பூமாலை","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Look at my Kumudha, Pandiyan. Protect her so that her life is not ruined. Both of you go to Madras. You can return after your enemy's anger has subsided......"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s047-u022","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s047-d017","speaker_label":"பாண்டியன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":54}]},"translation":{"english_text":"All right. We will do as you wish......"}}]}